[
 {
  "id": "2t08-q01",
  "chapterId": "puc2-statistics-08-statistical-inference-testing-of-hypothesis",
  "topicId": "puc2-statistics-08-statistical-inference-testing-of-hypothesis.t1",
  "stem": {
   "en": "A Type I error is committed when we:"
  },
  "options": [
   {
    "en": "accept H₀ when it is true"
   },
   {
    "en": "reject H₀ when it is false"
   },
   {
    "en": "accept H₀ when it is false"
   },
   {
    "en": "reject H₀ when it is true"
   }
  ],
  "answer": 3,
  "explanation": {
   "en": "Type I: rejecting a true null hypothesis. Type II: accepting a false one."
  },
  "exams": [
   "PUC"
  ],
  "difficulty": "easy",
  "tags": []
 },
 {
  "id": "2t08-q02",
  "chapterId": "puc2-statistics-08-statistical-inference-testing-of-hypothesis",
  "topicId": "puc2-statistics-08-statistical-inference-testing-of-hypothesis.t1",
  "stem": {
   "en": "The probability of a Type I error is called the:"
  },
  "options": [
   {
    "en": "critical value"
   },
   {
    "en": "power of the test"
   },
   {
    "en": "degrees of freedom"
   },
   {
    "en": "level of significance"
   }
  ],
  "answer": 3,
  "explanation": {
   "en": "α = P(Type I error) = P(reject H₀ | H₀ true) is the level of significance."
  },
  "exams": [
   "PUC"
  ],
  "difficulty": "easy",
  "tags": []
 },
 {
  "id": "2t08-q03",
  "chapterId": "puc2-statistics-08-statistical-inference-testing-of-hypothesis",
  "topicId": "puc2-statistics-08-statistical-inference-testing-of-hypothesis.t1",
  "stem": {
   "en": "For a two-tailed large-sample test at the 5% level of significance, the critical values of Z are:"
  },
  "options": [
   {
    "en": "±1.645"
   },
   {
    "en": "±1.96"
   },
   {
    "en": "±2.33"
   },
   {
    "en": "±2.58"
   }
  ],
  "answer": 1,
  "explanation": {
   "en": "Each tail has 2.5%; z = 1.96. (±2.58 is for 1%; 1.645 is one-tailed 5%.)"
  },
  "exams": [
   "PUC"
  ],
  "difficulty": "medium",
  "tags": []
 },
 {
  "id": "2t08-q04",
  "chapterId": "puc2-statistics-08-statistical-inference-testing-of-hypothesis",
  "topicId": "puc2-statistics-08-statistical-inference-testing-of-hypothesis.t1",
  "stem": {
   "en": "To test H₀: μ = 50 against H₁: μ > 50, we use:"
  },
  "options": [
   {
    "en": "no critical region"
   },
   {
    "en": "a right-tailed test"
   },
   {
    "en": "a left-tailed test"
   },
   {
    "en": "a two-tailed test"
   }
  ],
  "answer": 1,
  "explanation": {
   "en": "H₁ says \"greater than\", so the whole critical region lies in the right tail."
  },
  "exams": [
   "PUC"
  ],
  "difficulty": "medium",
  "tags": [],
  "solution": [
   {
    "en": "H₁ says \"greater than\", so the whole critical region lies in the right tail."
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "id": "2t08-q05",
  "chapterId": "puc2-statistics-08-statistical-inference-testing-of-hypothesis",
  "topicId": "puc2-statistics-08-statistical-inference-testing-of-hypothesis.t1",
  "stem": {
   "en": "A coin is tossed 4 times to test H₀: p = ½ against H₁: p = ¾ (p = P(head)). H₀ is rejected only if all 4 tosses are heads. The probability of a Type II error is:"
  },
  "options": [
   {
    "en": "81/256"
   },
   {
    "en": "175/256"
   },
   {
    "en": "1/16"
   },
   {
    "en": "15/16"
   }
  ],
  "answer": 1,
  "explanation": {
   "en": "Type II error = P(accept H₀ | H₁ true) = 1 − P(4 heads | p = ¾) = 1 − 81/256 = 175/256. (α = (½)⁴ = 1/16.)"
  },
  "exams": [
   "PUC"
  ],
  "difficulty": "hard",
  "tags": []
 },
 {
  "id": "2t08-q06",
  "chapterId": "puc2-statistics-08-statistical-inference-testing-of-hypothesis",
  "topicId": "puc2-statistics-08-statistical-inference-testing-of-hypothesis.t2",
  "stem": {
   "en": "A sample of 64 has mean 52. The population has s.d. 8. The test statistic for H₀: μ = 50 is:"
  },
  "options": [
   {
    "en": "Z = 16"
   },
   {
    "en": "Z = 4"
   },
   {
    "en": "Z = 2"
   },
   {
    "en": "Z = 0.25"
   }
  ],
  "answer": 2,
  "explanation": {
   "en": "Z = (x̄ − μ₀)/(σ/√n) = (52 − 50)/(8/8) = 2."
  },
  "exams": [
   "PUC"
  ],
  "difficulty": "easy",
  "tags": []
 },
 {
  "id": "2t08-q07",
  "chapterId": "puc2-statistics-08-statistical-inference-testing-of-hypothesis",
  "topicId": "puc2-statistics-08-statistical-inference-testing-of-hypothesis.t2",
  "stem": {
   "en": "In practice a sample is treated as large when its size n is:"
  },
  "options": [
   {
    "en": "more than 5"
   },
   {
    "en": "more than 30"
   },
   {
    "en": "less than 30"
   },
   {
    "en": "exactly 100"
   }
  ],
  "answer": 1,
  "explanation": {
   "en": "For n > 30 the sampling distribution of x̄ is close to normal (and s can replace σ), so the Z test is used."
  },
  "exams": [
   "PUC"
  ],
  "difficulty": "easy",
  "tags": []
 },
 {
  "id": "2t08-q08",
  "chapterId": "puc2-statistics-08-statistical-inference-testing-of-hypothesis",
  "topicId": "puc2-statistics-08-statistical-inference-testing-of-hypothesis.t2",
  "stem": {
   "en": "In a two-tailed large-sample test, Z = 2.2. Then H₀ is:"
  },
  "options": [
   {
    "en": "rejected at 5% but not rejected at 1%"
   },
   {
    "en": "not rejected at either level"
   },
   {
    "en": "rejected at both 5% and 1%"
   },
   {
    "en": "rejected at 1% but not at 5%"
   }
  ],
  "answer": 0,
  "explanation": {
   "en": "|Z| = 2.2 > 1.96 (reject at 5%) but 2.2 < 2.58 (do not reject at 1%)."
  },
  "exams": [
   "PUC"
  ],
  "difficulty": "medium",
  "tags": []
 },
 {
  "id": "2t08-q09",
  "chapterId": "puc2-statistics-08-statistical-inference-testing-of-hypothesis",
  "topicId": "puc2-statistics-08-statistical-inference-testing-of-hypothesis.t2",
  "stem": {
   "en": "Two samples of 100 each have means 24 and 22; both populations have s.d. 5. The value of Z for testing equality of means is about:"
  },
  "options": [
   {
    "en": "1.41"
   },
   {
    "en": "4.00"
   },
   {
    "en": "2.83"
   },
   {
    "en": "0.40"
   }
  ],
  "answer": 2,
  "explanation": {
   "en": "SE = √(25/100 + 25/100) = √0.5 = 0.707; Z = (24 − 22)/0.707 ≈ 2.83."
  },
  "exams": [
   "PUC"
  ],
  "difficulty": "medium",
  "tags": [],
  "solution": [
   {
    "en": "SE = √(25/100 + 25/100) = √0.5 = 0.707; Z = (24 − 22)/0.707 ≈ 2.83."
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "id": "2t08-q10",
  "chapterId": "puc2-statistics-08-statistical-inference-testing-of-hypothesis",
  "topicId": "puc2-statistics-08-statistical-inference-testing-of-hypothesis.t2",
  "stem": {
   "en": "A sample of 900 has mean 3.4 cm and s.d. 2.61 cm. For H₀: μ = 3.25 (two-tailed, 5%), the conclusion is:"
  },
  "options": [
   {
    "en": "Z ≈ 1.72; H₀ is rejected"
   },
   {
    "en": "Z ≈ 1.72; H₀ is not rejected"
   },
   {
    "en": "Z ≈ 5.17; H₀ is rejected"
   },
   {
    "en": "Z ≈ 0.06; H₀ is not rejected"
   }
  ],
  "answer": 1,
  "explanation": {
   "en": "SE = 2.61/√900 = 0.087; Z = 0.15/0.087 ≈ 1.72 < 1.96, so the sample is consistent with μ = 3.25."
  },
  "exams": [
   "PUC"
  ],
  "difficulty": "hard",
  "tags": []
 },
 {
  "id": "2t08-q11",
  "chapterId": "puc2-statistics-08-statistical-inference-testing-of-hypothesis",
  "topicId": "puc2-statistics-08-statistical-inference-testing-of-hypothesis.t3",
  "stem": {
   "en": "To test H₀: P = 0.5 with a sample of 100, the standard error of the sample proportion under H₀ is:"
  },
  "options": [
   {
    "en": "0.25"
   },
   {
    "en": "0.005"
   },
   {
    "en": "0.5"
   },
   {
    "en": "0.05"
   }
  ],
  "answer": 3,
  "explanation": {
   "en": "SE = √(P₀Q₀/n) = √(0.25/100) = 0.05."
  },
  "exams": [
   "PUC"
  ],
  "difficulty": "easy",
  "tags": []
 },
 {
  "id": "2t08-q12",
  "chapterId": "puc2-statistics-08-statistical-inference-testing-of-hypothesis",
  "topicId": "puc2-statistics-08-statistical-inference-testing-of-hypothesis.t3",
  "stem": {
   "en": "Samples of 100 and 200 have proportions 0.2 and 0.35. The pooled estimate of P is:"
  },
  "options": [
   {
    "en": "0.55"
   },
   {
    "en": "0.25"
   },
   {
    "en": "0.275"
   },
   {
    "en": "0.3"
   }
  ],
  "answer": 3,
  "explanation": {
   "en": "p̂ = (n₁p₁ + n₂p₂)/(n₁ + n₂) = (20 + 70)/300 = 0.3."
  },
  "exams": [
   "PUC"
  ],
  "difficulty": "easy",
  "tags": []
 },
 {
  "id": "2t08-q13",
  "chapterId": "puc2-statistics-08-statistical-inference-testing-of-hypothesis",
  "topicId": "puc2-statistics-08-statistical-inference-testing-of-hypothesis.t3",
  "stem": {
   "en": "A die is thrown 900 times and a six appears 180 times. The value of Z for testing that the die is fair is about:"
  },
  "options": [
   {
    "en": "1.20"
   },
   {
    "en": "2.68"
   },
   {
    "en": "0.20"
   },
   {
    "en": "5.00"
   }
  ],
  "answer": 1,
  "explanation": {
   "en": "Expected sixes = 150; SE = √(npq) = √(900 × 1/6 × 5/6) = √125 = 11.18; Z = (180 − 150)/11.18 ≈ 2.68."
  },
  "exams": [
   "PUC"
  ],
  "difficulty": "medium",
  "tags": []
 },
 {
  "id": "2t08-q14",
  "chapterId": "puc2-statistics-08-statistical-inference-testing-of-hypothesis",
  "topicId": "puc2-statistics-08-statistical-inference-testing-of-hypothesis.t3",
  "stem": {
   "en": "A firm claims that only 20% of its items are defective. A sample of 400 has 100 defectives. The value of Z is:"
  },
  "options": [
   {
    "en": "1.25"
   },
   {
    "en": "2.5"
   },
   {
    "en": "0.05"
   },
   {
    "en": "5"
   }
  ],
  "answer": 1,
  "explanation": {
   "en": "p = 0.25; SE = √(0.2 × 0.8/400) = 0.02; Z = (0.25 − 0.20)/0.02 = 2.5."
  },
  "exams": [
   "PUC"
  ],
  "difficulty": "medium",
  "tags": [],
  "solution": [
   {
    "en": "p = 0.25; SE = √(0.2 × 0.8/400) = 0.02; Z = (0.25 − 0.20)/0.02 = 2.5."
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "id": "2t08-q15",
  "chapterId": "puc2-statistics-08-statistical-inference-testing-of-hypothesis",
  "topicId": "puc2-statistics-08-statistical-inference-testing-of-hypothesis.t3",
  "stem": {
   "en": "In town A, 200 of 500 people like a product; in town B, 200 of 400. Using the pooled proportion, the value of Z for H₀: P₁ = P₂ is:"
  },
  "options": [
   {
    "en": "−0.1"
   },
   {
    "en": "−4.5"
   },
   {
    "en": "−1.5"
   },
   {
    "en": "−3.0"
   }
  ],
  "answer": 3,
  "explanation": {
   "en": "p₁ = 0.4, p₂ = 0.5, p̂ = 400/900 = 4/9. SE = √(4/9 × 5/9 × (1/500 + 1/400)) = √(0.2469 × 0.0045) = 0.0333. Z = −0.1/0.0333 = −3.0."
  },
  "exams": [
   "PUC"
  ],
  "difficulty": "hard",
  "tags": []
 },
 {
