  "tags": []
 },
 {
  "id": "2t08-q18",
  "chapterId": "puc2-statistics-08-statistical-inference-testing-of-hypothesis",
  "topicId": "puc2-statistics-08-statistical-inference-testing-of-hypothesis.t4",
  "stem": {
   "en": "In a paired t-test on 9 pairs, the mean difference is 2 and the s.d. of the differences (divisor n − 1) is 2. The value of t is:"
  },
  "options": [
   {
    "en": "6"
   },
   {
    "en": "1"
   },
   {
    "en": "9"
   },
   {
    "en": "3"
   }
  ],
  "answer": 3,
  "explanation": {
   "en": "t = d̄/(s_d/√n) = 2/(2/3) = 3, with 8 d.f."
  },
  "exams": [
   "PUC"
  ],
  "difficulty": "medium",
  "tags": []
 },
 {
  "id": "2t08-q19",
  "chapterId": "puc2-statistics-08-statistical-inference-testing-of-hypothesis",
  "topicId": "puc2-statistics-08-statistical-inference-testing-of-hypothesis.t4",
  "stem": {
   "en": "A sample of 16 has mean 53 and s = 8 (divisor n − 1). For H₀: μ = 50, the value of t and its d.f. are:"
  },
  "options": [
   {
    "en": "t = 1.5, 15 d.f."
   },
   {
    "en": "t = 6, 15 d.f."
   },
   {
    "en": "t = 1.5, 16 d.f."
   },
   {
    "en": "t = 0.375, 15 d.f."
   }
  ],
  "answer": 0,
  "explanation": {
   "en": "t = (53 − 50)/(8/√16) = 3/2 = 1.5, with 16 − 1 = 15 d.f."
  },
  "exams": [
   "PUC"
  ],
  "difficulty": "medium",
  "tags": [],
  "solution": [
   {
    "en": "t = (53 − 50)/(8/√16) = 3/2 = 1.5, with 16 − 1 = 15 d.f."
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "id": "2t08-q20",
  "chapterId": "puc2-statistics-08-statistical-inference-testing-of-hypothesis",
  "topicId": "puc2-statistics-08-statistical-inference-testing-of-hypothesis.t4",
  "stem": {
   "en": "Two independent samples: n₁ = 10, x̄₁ = 23, s₁² = 10 and n₂ = 12, x̄₂ = 20, s₂² = 12 (divisor n − 1). Using the pooled variance, t is about (t₀.₀₅ for 20 d.f. = 2.086):"
